# Admin Dashboard for SamadhanHub

## Overview

Add a **completely separate, protected Admin Dashboard** (`admin.html`) for SamadhanHub with its own login page, real-time problem tracking, and delete capabilities. All new code lives in **new files only** — the existing `index.html`, `app.js`, `database.js`, `index.css`, and `server.js` are **not modified**.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No changes to existing files** — all admin functionality is isolated to new files.
> Existing users browsing `index.html` will never see the admin panel.

> [!WARNING]
> **Plain-text credentials** — as requested, credentials are `admin.samadhan` / `1234`.
> This is a demo implementation. For production, always hash passwords and use secure sessions.

> [!NOTE]
> The admin dashboard routes are added to the existing `server.js` through a **separate middleware file** (`admin-routes.js`) that gets `require()`-d into `server.js`. This requires **one small addition** to `server.js` — a single `require` line.

